    {
      "block_id": "b_boundary",
      "type": "teach",
      "eyebrow": null,
      "title": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Why is a team example insufficient?"
        }
      ],
      "style": "standard",
      "visual": null,
      "evidence": null,
      "points": [
        {
          "point_id": "boundary_p0",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "boundary_s0",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A limited team’s success does not establish two independent creators; its members work within conditions and limits."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "boundary_p1",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "boundary_s1",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The example clarifies unrestricted authority; it does not make the creator resemble a referee or captain."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "boundary_p2",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "boundary_s2",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Now move from the team to the meaning of independence we examined earlier."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b_ex2",
      "type": "exercise",
      "exercise": {
        "exercise_id": "ex_u0_l05_02",
        "type": "true_false_reason",
        "concept_ids": [
          "con_u0_one_independent_creator"
        ],
        "prompt": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Evaluate the statement, then choose the reason."
          }
        ],
        "time_limit_ms": null,
        "scoring": {
          "accuracy": true,
          "combo": true,
          "layer": "apply"
        },
        "framing": null,
        "payload": {
          "statement": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two captains cooperating proves there can be two creators, both wholly independent and unrestricted."
            }
          ],
          "reasons": [
            {
              "option_id": "opt_a",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Because ships need sailors."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "option_id": "opt_b",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Because this teamwork includes division and shared limits."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "option_id": "opt_c",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Because every team always fails."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b_independence",
      "type": "teach",
      "eyebrow": null,
      "title": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Test “unrestricted”"
        }
      ],
      "style": "standard",
      "visual": null,
      "evidence": null,
      "points": [
        {
          "point_id": "independence_p0",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "independence_s0",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Now suppose two creators, each with power the other cannot restrict."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "independence_p1",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "independence_s1",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "If two wanted an outcome and its opposite simultaneously, both wishes could not be fulfilled."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "independence_p2",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "independence_s2",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "If another prevents one from carrying out a choice, that one lacks power unrestricted by others."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "independence_p3",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "independence_s3",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Saying they always agree does not, by itself, explain why disagreement would be impossible."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        },
        {
          "point_id": "independence_p4",
          "sentence": {
            "sentence_id": "independence_s4",
            "spans": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "This checks the idea’s conditions; it does not claim we observed creators disagreeing."
              }
            ],
            "source_ids": []
          },
          "visual_params": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b_ex3",
      "type": "exercise",
      "exercise": {
        "exercise_id": "ex_u0_l05_03",
        "type": "spot_error",
        "concept_ids": [
          "con_u0_one_independent_creator"
        ],
        "prompt": [
          {
            "type": "text",
